# Line-ending policy.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS: every tracked text file in this repo is currently stored
# with DOUBLED line endings (\r\r\n). They were committed containing CRLF,
# and `core.autocrlf=true` on a Windows clone then converts the \n again on
# checkout, giving \r\r\n in the working tree. MSVC reports the stray CR as
#     warning C4335: Mac file format detected
# on essentially every file, on every build.
#
# This file fixes the policy going FORWARD: `text=auto` tells git to store
# these types with LF in the object database and convert on checkout, so new
# and re-added files stop compounding.
#
# It does NOT fix the 102 files already stored wrong -- that needs a
# one-shot `git add --renormalize .`, which touches every file in the repo
# and so wants its own commit on a quiet day, not one mixed in with feature
# work. Tracked as an issue; see the repo issue list for "line endings".

*                text=auto

# Explicit for the source we compile, so this survives someone narrowing the
# catch-all above.
*.cpp            text
*.h              text
*.md             text
*.txt            text
*.cmake          text
*.yml            text
*.py             text
*.dat            text

# Shell scripts must keep LF even on Windows checkouts -- a CR in a shebang
# line makes the interpreter path unrunnable.
*.sh             text eol=lf

# Windows batch files need CRLF; a lone LF can break `goto` and label parsing
# in cmd.exe.
*.bat            text eol=crlf

# Binary -- never touch these.
*.png            binary
*.jpg            binary
*.ico            binary
*.qm             binary
*.db             binary
